window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY=window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY||{};window.HELLSCRIPT_WIKI_HISTORY["dependents"]=[{"body": "# D4 skill tree: dependents outside the combat engine (read-only audit)\n\nPrefixes (absolute): W=/Users/t8g-2410-pn-005/Documents/MyProject/HELLSCRIPT/wt-d4-skill-plan; RC=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Core; RP=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation; RR=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Resources; T=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Tests/Editor; E=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Editor. Counts are my own greps unless marked (tool).\n\n## 0. Reading the inventory\n- Tool: 12,680 refs/475 files; groups 1-5 = 4,609 refs/133 files (`--check` exits 1). About 197 refs in 13 files are SVG path data (`M12 2 ...`, zero quoted ids): Prototypes RuneBoard html 148, Jeweler 12, RiftEntry/ui.js 5, AspectStone ui+svg 6, TrainingGround 8, Blacksmith 11, DailyQuests 3, tools/blacksmith/export-resources.cjs 4. Real prototype hits: SkillTree/*, HuntEdict/*, RiftVictory/{ui.js,build.cjs,source-manifest.json}, RiftEntry/engine.test.cjs, AspectStone/catalog.json.\n- It counts removed ids only. Blind spots, covered below: kept ids whose rules change (W01 becomes T2; A06/M07 change meaning), the version gate `ClassSkillTree.Uses` (55 sites/29 files), `ClassSkillTree.Unlocked` (17 non-smoke lines/11 files), level 30/40 literals, UI element names tutorials aim at.\n\n## A. Old skill window(s)\n**Builders.** No standalone skill window exists; the tree is the \"skills\" tab of the unified edict window.\n- RP/HuntEdictWindow.cs:40-51 `Open`: `Session.UseSkillTree(hero)` :48; `ContentWindowHost.Attach(view,view.HandleBack)` :49; `StoreViewBinding.Attach(view,store,view.Repaint,()=>!HasDialog&&!HuntEdictOrderCard.Dragging,view.DisclosureDisplayKey)` :50 (key holds `StoreViewBinding.Key(hero.build.classSkills)`, HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:99-103). `DrawSkills()` :112; `HandleBack` :59-60; `SelectTab` :142; `SelectSkillPage` :152; draft model with Save/Revert footer :124-135, `Change` :173-179.\n- RP/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs (455 lines): `SelectSkill` :23; `DrawSkills` :35; `DrawTreePanel` :66 (list mode :71-76; tree mode :77-104 with Art/SkillTree/tree-backdrop + skill-point-gem); `DrawTreeCanvas` :106 and `DrawTreeNode` :208 (`SkillTreeLayout`, SkillTreeGraphic.cs:13-20); `ChangeRank/Equip/Unequip` :251-262; slot bubble :263-346; `OpenSkillPolicy` :348; `DrawSkillBar` :361 (4 actives + ultimate, `NodeFrame` :233-244); `DrawSkillDetails` :399 (inspector; buttons `edict-skill-rank-down|up|equip` :441-443; unlock rows :430-434).\n- Policy page HuntEdictWindow.SkillPresets.cs:54 (back button \"스킬 트리로\" :59; order :163-167; options :169-184); CombatPreview.cs (text \"레벨 40 · 스킬 1등급\" :90).\n- `ShowLegacyEdictEditor` RP/GameUI.EdictEditor.cs:27: private `Base(\"edict\")` page; `SkillName` = `game.catalog.skills.Single` :21 throws for ids outside the 18 legacy slots. Reached only from its own legacy share page (GameUI.EdictShare.cs:28) and 13 smokes: Runtime{Blizzard,Chain,Fireball,MageBasic,Nova,Ranger,Shield,Slam,Teleport,WarriorAttack,WarriorSupport}Smoke.cs:33, RuntimeTargetSmoke.cs:74, RuntimeLanguageSmoke.cs:183. Not tree UI; keep while those smokes live.\n- Other pickers: rift entry RP/RiftEntryWindow.cs:336-356 + Popups.cs:75-125 (learned candidates; `Store.ReplaceRiftSkill` RC/GameStore.RiftEntry.cs:39-51); training lobby TrainingGroundWindow.Skills.cs:12-62.\n\n**Entry points.**\n- Whole edict window: hub RP/GameUI.cs:242-244 and :446; dock GameUI.ContentDock.cs:31; observation menu GameUI.GlobalHud.cs:130; GameUI.{RiftVictory.cs:11, TrainingEquipment.cs:31, Comparison.cs:210-216 (loads a recorded loadout as draft), PuzzleHub.cs:41, Puzzle.cs:44, PuzzleOpening.cs:44, Tutorials.cs:105-110 (guides F06/H07/H08 target \"skills\"), FirstPlay.cs:19-23 (`SelectTab`+`SelectSkillPage(true)`+`SelectSkill(id)`), TrainingGround.cs:38-42 (`OpenSkillPolicy`)}.\n- Direct tree page (`ShowEdictSkillTree` GameUI.HuntEdict.cs:69): RiftEntryWindow.cs:355; SkillPresets.cs:59; HuntEdictWindow.cs:60. Not in plan 9.1: HuntEdictWindow.Presets.cs:96-99 (a stored preset whose allocation fails validation jumps to the skills tab). Recommended mode keeps the manage page editable (HuntEdictWindow.cs:85,147,176). No NPC/plaza route exists.\n- Smoke flags: one class gates eight (RP/RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:44: SkillTree, SkillReset, SkillMenu, SkillPreset, SkillCombatPreview, SkillIdentity, RegressionRepair, EdictSections); also `-hellscriptClassSkillSmoke` (RC/ClassSkillNativeSmoke.cs:38), BattleQuickEdit (RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke.cs:213), QuickPreset, GuideTutorial, Tutorial.\n\n**Reads/writes.** Reads `store.Data`, `hero.build.classSkills`, rune levels `new HeroStats(hero,false,store.Data.runes).runeSkillLevels` (Skills.cs:19), `ClassSkillTree/ClassSkills/ClassSkillOptions`, `HuntEdictProgression`, `PuzzleTutorial`, `SkillProgressionInfo.Compare` (Skills.cs:436-438). Writes only via the commit lambda RP/GameUI.HuntEdict.cs:25-52 (4 contexts: comparison `ValidateB`+`ApplyHuntEdict`; training/puzzle `ApplyTrainingHuntEdict` or sandbox `game.PuzzleStore.CommitHuntEdict`; guide; normal/live `GameStore.CommitHuntEdict` RC/GameStore.HuntEdict.cs:9-62 with `PrepareHuntEdictChange`/`PrepareSuspendedHuntEdictChange`), plus `SetRecommendedEdict` (GameStore.Edict.cs:9) and immediate policy saves (`SaveSkillPolicy` RC/HuntEdictLoadout.cs:126-137). Every store edit API needs the selected hero (GameStore.HuntEdict.cs:13, GameStore.Edict.cs:13,30,61, GameStore.RiftEntry.cs:43): plan D2's per-hero tabs need a new per-hero commit.\n\n**Delete / keep / flag.**\n- Delete at phase 7: Skills.cs:66-104 tree branch and :106-230, `BandNames` :24, unlock rows :430-434, `SkillTreeLayout`, RR/Data/ClassSkillTree.json, Art/SkillTree/tree-backdrop + skill-point-gem (+E/ResourceTextureBudget.cs:33,76), en.txt:5286-5336, Prototypes/SkillTree, tools/build_skill_tree.cjs, RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke* (954 lines), SkillTreeIntegrationTests layout test (:207-214), caller-less `GameStore.CommitClassSkills` (RC/ClassSkillCodec.cs:69-81).\n- Keep: `SkillTreeGraphic` (glyphs HuntEdictWindow.Glyphs.cs:10, diagrams SkillPresetExampleView.cs:106), skill bar, slot bubble, policy page, order editor, Art/SkillTree/node-frame-*.\n- Keep or port: the tutorial list-mode UI (`DrawAvailableSkills` HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:35-45; inspector +/equip; guards Skills.cs:23,251-252). Plan 12 says only \"tree and inspector\"; four tutorial files aim at these names (C).\n- Flag at: `ShowEdictSkillTree`, `DrawSkills`, RiftEntryWindow.cs:355, FirstPlay.cs:22, SkillPresets.cs:59 (label must stop saying \"skill tree\"), Presets.cs:99, Tutorials.cs:110, TrainingGround.cs:41.\n- Hazard, not in plan: the edict window's `HuntEdictEditSession` is built once (HuntEdictWindow.cs:48) and refreshed only by its own commit (GameStore.HuntEdict.cs:59); `StoreViewBinding` just calls `Repaint` (:50,138-141), which redraws the stale draft. A D4 window above it that commits would be reverted by the parent's next Save, and the parent's equip bar shows old ranks. The parent must `AcceptSaved`/rebuild after each child commit.\n\n## B. Battle quick edit, HUD, recommended skills (PR #83: HuntEdictQuickMenu, GameUI.{EdictQuick,SkillQuick}, GlobalHudView, HoldPress, RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke; the potion quick files hold no skill logic)\n**Today.** HUD slots: 3 potions, 4 actives, 1 ultimate (RP/GlobalHudView.cs:58-60,128-131). Tap -> `SkillSlotTapped` (RP/GameUI.SkillQuick.cs:21-39): candidates = learned, unequipped skills of the slot kind (`HuntEdictQuickMenu.SkillCandidates` RC/HuntEdictQuickMenu.cs:57-58; slot 4 = ultimates), then, while a point is free, level/lineage-unlocked rank-0 skills (`LearnableSkills` :60-61, drawn dim, SkillQuick.cs:36). Tap a candidate -> `EquipQuickSkill` :84-96 (`ClassSkillTree.Equip` + `CommitHuntEdict(session,catalog,game.Combat,true)`). Hold (0.3 s + 0.7 s gauge) -> `ShowSkillPopup` :97-126 (`ClassSkillDisplay.Description`; \"레벨 올리기\" = `RankQuickSkill` :127-137, base +1 only; \"장착\"; use presets). Only in ordinary rift fights (`QuickBattleEditable`, GameUI.EdictQuick.cs:24-32) or the guide stage; `SkillQuickAvailable` (SkillQuick.cs:19) uses `ClassSkillTree.Uses` (= v3/v4), so a v5 loadout silently disables it. Display: `GlobalHudSnapshot.Read` fills skills only for v3/v4 (RP/GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:86-103); `HudSlotState` (:9-14) has no rank/modifier; icon `SkillIconAssets.TryResolve` (GlobalHudView.cs:140, SkillIconView.cs:57-71); cooldown = radial `Cover` + `TimeLabel` (GlobalHudView.cs:143-146).\nThe HUD does not choose \"recommended skills\". The recommended things are: `useRecommendedEdict` (RC/HuntEdictDefaults.cs:11-34: keeps allocation/slots, clears `options`/`presetSelections`, automatic = all); `FirstPlayRecommendation` skill steps (RC/FirstPlayRecommendation.cs:28-40); legacy \"현재 레벨 추천\" `BehaviorPresets.ForLevel` (GameUI.Growth.cs:49-72; level clamp 1-30, BehaviorPresets.cs:13; not tree-aware); 122 use presets (RR/HuntEdictQuickPresets.json) and the \"identity\" order (RC/HuntEdictQuickPresets.cs:112).\n**Changes.**\n- Modifier chosen: add `rank/modifier/modifierRank` to `ClassSkillStatus` (RC/ClassSkillReadModel.cs:7-14) and `HudSlotState`. `TryResolve` returns false for `W01-3` (no `ClassSkills.Find`; a 5-char id misses the legacy branches :63-70): add a `<base>-<n>` branch (art `Art/ClassSkillIcons/<Class>/<id>`) if a badge is wanted. Put modifier name + shape sentence + n/5 into `ClassSkillDisplay.Description/Activation` (RC/ClassSkillDisplay.cs:9-31), used by the HUD (GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:94,99), popup (SkillQuick.cs:102), rift-entry popup (RiftEntryWindow.Popups.cs:105-107). Popup: \"+1 on the chosen modifier / pick one\" and the plan's blocked reasons; swap/refund only in town (D3). First fix `ClassSkillTree.Display`: its regex matches `A06` inside `A06-2` (ClassSkillTree.cs:119-120). Other icon/name sites: TrainingGroundWindow.Skills.cs:53-58, RiftSkillShareView.cs:35, TrainingChartView.cs:62,113-114, StatusStripView.cs:109, GameUI.GlobalHud.cs:51-55, toast SkillQuick.cs:94; `TrainingGround.DescribeChanges` (RC/TrainingGround.cs:214-229) should diff modifier/rank. HUD badge vs name is undecided in the plan.\n- Unlearned: restate the v4 rule \"unlearned cannot be equipped\" (RC/ClassSkills.cs:123) for v5; rank 0 clears the slot (ClassSkillTree.cs:114-115) and must be refused while the modifier holds rank; candidates already skip rank 0 (HuntEdictQuickMenu.cs:58). `Unlocked(load,level,id)` is level+lineage; the (hero,level,id) overload (ClassSkillTree.cs:60; Tutorials.Progress.cs:17) cannot express tier gates. HUD `locked` (GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:94) loses meaning.\n- Ultimate rank 3: `RankScale` is 1 for ultimates (RC/ClassSkills.cs:65; used ClassSkillDisplay.cs:19, ClassSkillReadModel.cs:22,26). Cooldown 60/55/50 reaches the HUD via `CS.ultimateTotal` (ClassSkillReadModel.cs:25; `Max(45,cd)` at CombatSimulation.ClassSkills.cs:163); persistence accepts totals 45-60 (ClassSkillPersistence.cs:26) and rankScale 1..1.401 (:37), so +20%/rank (1.4 at rank 3) fits by 0.001. Replace \"Lv.40\" gates by \"T5 open or learned\": GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:99, HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:33, RiftEntryWindow.cs:338,345,349,356, TrainingGroundWindow.Skills.cs:42, Tutorials.cs:56,214, en.txt:5758,5837.\n\n## C. Tutorials and guide\nLive flows: guide stage (flow 6; new accounts, warrior only: RC/GameStore.Guide.cs:11, RP/GameController.Tutorials.cs:16); puzzle (flow 5; accounts mid-puzzle plus every replay/hub: GameController.Tutorials.cs:17-20,50); pit/starter (old checkpoints only, RC/Tutorials.cs:153-169).\n- Guide stage: `GuideTutorial.Skill=\"W01\"` (RC/GuideTutorial.cs:13), `BarePowers`=`ResetAllocation` (:52-57), `LessonDone` :77, `StartGuideTutorial` GameStore.Guide.cs:18, copy/anchors \"회오리\", \"스킬 포인트가 1점\" (RP/GameUI.GuideTutorial.cs:36,70,94-102; `edict-quick-skill-*` names), fingerprint \"tutorial-v6\" (GuideTutorial.cs:12-13; mismatching checkpoints are dropped, Tutorials.cs:163). W01 is T2 (gate 2; skill_tree_d4.json rules.tierGates [0,2,6,11,40]), so the level-1 point cannot buy it. Rebase on W09 (plan D7): change `Skill`, copy, Version/Fingerprint; teach W01 only at 2+1 points (hero level 3); update RuntimeGuideTutorialSmoke, GuideTutorialTests (3).\n- Prologue/starter/pit: `PrologueSkill/StarterComparison` hard-code W01/A01/M01 + presets stand/edge, elite/steady, steady/pack (RC/Tutorials.cs:98-101). Consumers: `ProloguePowers` (GameStore.Tutorials.cs:33-48: `ChangeRank` on a T2 skill at level 1 throws), `CanAdvancePrologueLesson` :93-100, CombatPreviewSession.cs:41-49, CombatSimulation.SkillPreview.cs:16-26, HuntEdictProgression.cs:101-102,165-168 (level-1 \"first skill only\", `owner.level>=2`), HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:37-38,90-98. Needs a T1 starter per class: W09/W08, A07/A14, M07 (mage has one T1 active).\n- Overlays aim at old-window element names: RP/GameUI.TutorialStaging.cs:259-323, PuzzleOpening.cs:50-61, TutorialPit.cs:113-122, TutorialComparison.cs:10-29 (`edict-skill-<id>`, `edict-skill-rank-up|equip`, `edict-active-slot-0`, `edict-slot-policy`, `edict-policy-back`, `edict-preset-tab-*`, `edict-preset-activate`). Keep the lesson-mode UI or retarget four files.\n- Puzzle (16 levels): RR/PuzzleTutorial.json kits, e.g. level 7: W01 W02 WP01 W03 / A01 A02 AP01 A03 A04 / M01 M02 MP01 M03 M04 at hero level <=7. W02 is T4, A03/A04/M04 T3, WP01 unlocks Lv4 (hero is 3 at puzzle 4), MP01 is removed (13 refs). Granted by `ClassSkillTree.ChangeRank` (RC/PuzzleTutorial.cs:100 `Instructor`, :150-163 `StartPowers`), validated :208-211 (`rank>1` forbidden): needs a kit/exempt API. Also GameUI.Puzzle.cs:18-30,57,72-76, CombatSimulation.Tutorial.cs:133,148,170. Saved loadouts: `puzzle.levels[].kitHero` (replay source PuzzleTutorial.cs:225-228), T/Fixtures/PuzzleAfterL8-{Mage,Ranger,Warrior}.json (553 refs; PuzzleContentTests.cs:94, PuzzleTutorialCoreTests.cs:26).\n- F06/H07/H08/H17: RC/Tutorials.cs:33 (F06 copy \"2레벨부터 받는 스킬 포인트\"), :55-56 (H08 \"레벨 40\"), :214-217; Tutorials.Progress.cs:10-18 (F06 = open active never slotted, level>=2), :51-59 (H07 on `Spent` growth, H08 on ultimate); TutorialChapters.cs C05 {F06,H07}; FirstPlayRecommendation.cs:28-40; docs Tutorial_Progression.md:15,67-80. New rule: the first T2 skill needs 2 points in T1/passives = hero level 3 for every class, so the \"level-2 point\" premise (Tutorials.Progress.cs:10-12) is false and `NewSkills` needs the allocation, not level. `ClassPracticeLesson.cs:9,28` (A02/M02, both T2) must test \"learned\".\n- New-player start: `StartNewHeroesWithoutSkills`+`ActivateSkillTrees` (RC/GameStore.SkillTree.cs:13-47; callers GameController.cs:65,238, GameController.Accounts.cs:23, GameUI.RiftKeeper.cs:15; skips heroes with a suspended run :30,34) emit v3/v4.\n\n## D. Auto-battle / Hunt Edict\n- Two layers. Legacy V2 document: 4 slots, `skillOrder`, option sets for 01-06 only (`HuntEdict.SkillIds` RC/HuntEdict.cs:56; HuntEdictV2.Options.cs:40-129; rule conditions, EdictValidation.cs:53); tree loadouts project into it only for `LegacyIndex>=0` ids (RC/ClassSkills.cs:150-161). Of 30 retained actives 17 are legacy-index; 13 are not (W08 W09 W17 W18 A07 A14 A17 A18 M07 M08 M11 M17 M18): they use `ClassSkillOptions` (55 groups/166 choices; 25/74 sit on removed actives) and cannot be picked by `survival.defenseSkill|escapeSkill|fallbackSkill`, `explore.cursedDefense` (EdictOptions.cs:63,70; HUD choices from `edict.slots`, HuntEdictHudRows.cs:23), which still list M05.\n- Removed-id hits: HuntEdictV2.Options.cs:117-120 (M05), HuntEdictV2.Order.cs:49 (`BuffSkill`), :51,63,89 (compiled `edict:M05`, slot 16), HuntEdictV2.Availability.cs:50 (needs WP03), :73, :75; `UnlockLevel` use :27,35; HuntEdictV2.cs:91,94.\n- Presets/scenarios change atomically: RR/HuntEdictQuickPresets.json 211 presets (122 skill, 50 on removed ids; 76 global; 9 basic; 4 order); RR/SkillPresetScenarios.json 122 scenarios (50 removed); `SkillPresetScenario.All` throws unless every non-passive catalog skill has exactly one scenario per preset (RC/SkillPresetScenario.cs:52-53). SkillPresetExampleView.cs:62-98 has M05/M13 scenes.\n- Saved policy ids: `presetSelections` for `skill/<removed>` make `ClassSkillLoadout.Canonical` throw (RC/HuntEdictSkillPresets.cs:19,22-35), unknown `options` throw (ClassSkillOptions.cs:46-52). Plan 7 filters `order/automatic/options` only; also filter `presetSelections`, `legacyEdict` (slots, skillOrder, survival refs), `actives`, `ultimate`, `ranks`.\n- `ClassSkillValidationBuild`: 30 builds in ClassSkills.json (29 touch removed ids); `CreateClassSkillValidation` (RC/CombatSimulation.ClassSkillValidation.cs:29-58) writes level 40 + free-form actives/passives/ultimate under `classSkillValidation`; `CreateSkillPreview` does likewise (CombatSimulation.SkillPreview.cs:31-38). Tier/point rules need an explicit fixture bypass. Users: T/ClassSkillCompatibilityTests.cs:18-26, ClassSkillPassiveMeasurement.cs:188.\n- Recommended-edict defaults: `HuntEdictDefaults.Skills` keeps allocation (a modifier rides along); `SetRecommendedEdict` is selected-hero only (GameStore.Edict.cs:9-22).\n\n## E. Tooling, docs, localization, art\n- CI .github/workflows/class-skills.yml:22-29: `class_skill_runtime.py check` (111/123/60/55, :24-25,42); `class_skills.py check` (16/19/2 per class :42; 111/141 :38; ultimate unlock 40 rank 1 :48; 30 builds :69; sha256 of GameCatalog.cs, SkillEffects.cs, SkillProgression.cs, Itemization.cs, LegendaryPowers.json, ClassSetReference/catalog.json :97-113); `class_skill_options.py check` (55/166 :10,49); `class_skill_reports.py check` (90 builds + 18 `M13=`/`W02=` runs :25-34); `node Prototypes/SkillTree/build.cjs` + `git diff --exit-code` (embeds sha256 of ClassSkills.json and Docs/Design/ClassSkills/catalog.json, build.cjs:5-13); `node tools/build_skill_tree.cjs --check`; `node Prototypes/SkillTree/engine.test.cjs`. All fail on the first data edit. shared-ui.yml:19 runs `check_ui_contract.py --verify` (ADAPTERS :16-23; rules :63-77: unregistered `*Window`, Canvas owners, hex literals).\n- Pipeline: Docs/Design/ClassSkills/{catalog,runtime_parameters,use_options}.json -> RR/Data/ClassSkills.json; Prototypes/SkillTree -> RR/Data/ClassSkillTree.json. Generated docs: Docs/Design/HELLSCRIPT_{Warrior,Ranger,Mage}_Skills(.en).md, HELLSCRIPT_Skill_Equipment(.en).md, Class_Skill_Use_Policies(.en).md. Inventory group 6: 342 files/8,071 refs.\n- balance_1000.py:222-231 (sha256 of ClassSkills.cs, GameStore.SkillTree.cs, ClassSkillTree.cs, GameStore.cs, Economy.cs, HeroStats.Blacksmith.cs, ClassSkills.json, ClassSkillTree.json); Balance1000/production_skill_tree_audit.json (`skillTreeVersion:3, levelCap:40`) read by test_balance_1000.py:19-25. wiki.py:143-163, :302 (`skills:18,passives:18`), :690-714 (`tree_levels[id]` KeyError; titles \"108/164/55\" :712-714,796-799); test_wiki.py:37-46,134-135 (:84's 108 = legendaries, unaffected). generate_sfx.py:83-86 + T/SoundBankTests.cs:150 + ClassSkillRuntimeTests.Audio.cs:12 (a `skill.<id>` sound per non-passive skill); audit_equipment_art.py:51; class_set_reference.py:38,55 and legendary_catalog.py:30 (ids limited to 01-06).\n- Localization: en.txt:5286-5336 (old tree), 20 lines naming removed skills (503-505, 1218-1220, 1679-1680, 1802-1803, 2126, 2133, 6460; :124 WP03), level-40 lines 5758, 5837, 6356. Names/descriptions live in ClassSkills.json (name/nameEn), GameCatalog.cs:466-484 and `GameCatalog.Passives` via `Loc.T` (GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:72), not in en.txt.\n- Art: 37 icons per class in RR/Art/ClassSkillIcons (A06/M07 are overwritten: check `.meta` guid); fallbacks RR/Art/GlobalHUD/passive-* and Art/SkillAtlas.png (SkillIconView.cs:63-70; T/HuntEdictFoundationTests.cs:215-231 loops the 12 legacy ids per class); Docs/Art/ClassSkillIcons/manifest.json (111; assemble_manifest.py:15 `pass==111`); E/ResourceTextureBudget.cs:24 already covers `Art/ClassSkillIcons/`; BuildResourceTests.cs:11, RuntimeBuildResourceSmoke.cs:21.\n- asmdef: one runtime asmdef (Core+Presentation+Runes) and Hellscript.Tests.asmdef absorb new files; only `.meta` files are needed.\n\n## F. Smokes and EditMode tests\nSmokes: 158 files (157 RP/Runtime*Smoke*.cs + RC/ClassSkillNativeSmoke.cs): 30 touch the old window API, 7 only removed ids, 8 only tree API, 113 untouched.\n- Replace: RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke{,.CombatPreview,.Identity,.Presets,.Sections}.cs (954 lines, 8 flags) -> `-hellscriptSkillTreeD4Smoke`. First move `ExistingTrees`/`OpenEdict` (RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:23-37; builds `version=3` loadouts) to a shared fixture: 8 call sites in 7 files (RuntimeRiftEntrySmoke .cs/.Portal/.Pickers/.Preparation/.Repeat, EdictQuickPresetSmoke:105, TrainingGroundSmoke:121).\n- Port: EdictQuickPreset (18 hits), Tutorial{,.Puzzle,.Pit}, GuideTutorial, RecommendedEquipment.Controls, RiftEntry*, BattleQuickEdit{,.Order} (setup learns every \"unlocked\" skill, :227-234), EdictContract, Edict, Language, UiStyle, TrainingGround{,.SafeDodge}, TrainingEquipment, Target; id-bound: ClassSkillNativeSmoke (25 refs), Shield (M05/MP04), Ranger, WarriorAttack, ArtGallery, RiftVictory{,.Actions}, Effect, Passive, Charge (text).\n- Stay while `ShowLegacyEdictEditor` stays: Blizzard, Chain, Fireball, MageBasic, Nova, Slam, Teleport, WarriorSupport.\nEditMode: 249 files, 4,518 cases (~2,731 methods); 29 files/462 refs name removed ids (101 methods in 27 files); ~64 files/~248 methods use tree/tutorial/preset APIs.\n- Delete or rewrite (pin old rules): SkillTreeIntegrationTests (17 methods/42 cases; layout :207-214, counts :59,68), ClassSkillRuntimeTests.cs:56-59 (37/16/19), ClassSkillBoundaryTests.cs:48,69 (37 ranks, cap 30), ClassSkillPassiveTests.cs:124, ClassSkillPolicyTests.cs:58 (55 options), HuntEdictFoundationTests.cs:198-231.\n- Port (methods): GuideTutorial 3, TutorialProgression 18, FirstPlaySkill 6, FirstPlayExperience 7, TutorialChapter 6, TutorialHeroSlots 9, Puzzle{Content 5, Opening 9, TutorialCore 10, Graduation 15, Level 1}, HuntEdict{Progression 20, QuickMenu 9, QuickPreset 5, SkillPreset 9, Overview 10, SuspendedSave 6, Defaults 5}, SkillPresetCombatPreview 10, TrainingGround 20, TrainingGroundUi 12, RecommendedEquipment (codec :210,239-242), ClassSkillCompatibility 7.\n- Engine-bound, id-bound (out of scope): ClassSkillPolicy 12 methods, ClassSkillRuntimeTests.Identity 12, .Contributions 9, EdictShield 9, Effect 8, EdictResponse 7, others 1-4 each.\n- Stay: the rest (~2,480 methods), incl. `ContentTestAccounts` (62 files; legacy 18-slot path).\n\n## G. Fifteen places most likely to be forgotten (risk order)\n1. CI class-skills.yml (7 steps, E) goes red on the first catalog edit; Prototypes/SkillTree/build.cjs hashes ClassSkills.json.\n2. Save read throws for any v3/v4 loadout invalid in the new catalog: RC/GameStore.cs:159-163 (`hero.build`), :166 and :413-414 (suspended run), :170-187 (`presets[]`). Migrate before `Normalize` and cover every holder: `edictPresets[].loadout`, `edictLegacyBuild`, `trainingGround.records[].{previous,best}.loadout` (RC/TrainingGround.cs:33), `trainingComparison.baselineHeroJson`, `puzzle.levels[].kitHero`, `tutorialRun/tutorialSlots`; filter presetSelections/options/legacyEdict too (D). Plan 7 names `hero` and `order/automatic/options` only.\n3. Suspended run/portal: `ActivateSkillTrees` skips such heroes (GameStore.SkillTree.cs:30,34) while `ClassSkillPersistence.ValidateRun` throws on cooldown/cast/effect ids of removed skills (:33,37,42,48: W15 loan, M13 channel, W02/M13 intent): the portal run becomes unreadable.\n4. `ClassSkillTree.Uses` (v3|v4, ClassSkillTree.cs:25) gates 55 sites: HUD (GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:86), quick edit (SkillQuick.cs:19), `UsesTree`, HeroStats (Economy.cs:129), TrainingGround.cs:37,214, ClassSkills.cs:60: all go silent for v5.\n5. Two writers of `classSkills` (stale parent session, A hazard) and no per-hero commit (A); the commit lambda has 4 contexts (GameUI.HuntEdict.cs:25-52).\n6. Tutorial overlays bound to old element names + the lesson-mode UI (C).\n7. Hand-built fixtures assume free-form loadouts: RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:29-37, CombatSimulation.SkillPreview.cs:31-38, ClassSkillValidation.cs:33-39, PuzzleTutorial.cs:95-108,147-176, GuideTutorial.cs:52-57, GameStore.Tutorials.cs:33-48, PuzzleAfterL8 fixtures: give the v5 validator one explicit kit/fixture path.\n8. Share codes: `ClassSkillCodec.Decode` demands byte-exact canonical JSON (RC/ClassSkillCodec.cs:19-52; wrapped by HuntEdictPresetCodec.cs:29-36,53-54), so new `modifier` fields break every existing HED4/HED5 code unless an old-wire branch exists (tests ClassSkillBoundaryTests.cs:46-49, RecommendedEquipmentTests.cs:210,239-242, ClassSkillPassiveTests.cs:124-132).\n9. Pinned counts: ClassSkills.cs:52-56 (111/123/60, unlock<=40), SkillPresetScenario.cs:52-53, ClassSkillOptions.cs:46 (<=55), plus E/F. Old and new catalogs cannot coexist behind the flag until versioned (6 key passives already push 111 up).\n10. 30/40 literals missing from plan 4: ClassSkills.cs:137,147; GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:99; HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:33; RiftEntryWindow.cs:345,349,356; GameUI.Growth.cs:20,36 (cap 30); BehaviorPresets.cs:13; CombatSimulation.SkillPreview.cs:31, ClassSkillValidation.cs:33; HuntEdictWindow.CombatPreview.cs:90; ClassSkillTree.cs:42 (cache key `class*41+level`); CombatSimulation.cs:14-15 + Economy.cs:128 (non-owned training uses LevelCap as hero level); Tutorials.cs:56,214.\n11. `ClassSkillTree.UnlockLevel` (:30) feeds engine LEVEL_LOCK (CombatSimulation.ClassSkills.cs:24) and HuntEdictV2Availability (:27); tiers have no unlock level.\n12. ID plumbing: `SkillIconAssets.TryResolve`, `ClassSkillTree.Display` regex, `ClassSkills.Find` null for `W01-3`; `ClassSkills.Find(skill).legacy` NREs for scopes naming removed ids (HuntEdictQuickPresets.cs:122,185, HuntEdictSkillPresets.cs:75).\n13. Legacy screens under-report because `build.activeSkills` holds only legacy ids: GameUI.SettingsInformation.cs:31-34, Presets.cs:88, Growth.cs:19-49, History.cs:16-17; legendary \"requiredSkill Lv.N\" text (InventoryLayout.cs:188-193); RuneMasteryCatalog.cs:59-61 and `runeSkillLevels[18]` (gear/rune +rank reaches only the 17 retained legacy-index actives; plan D5).\n14. Presentation keyed by old ids: GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:135-147, GameAudio.Combat.cs:21-27 + RR/Audio/Sfx/bank.json (30 refs), WorldView.SkillFx.cs:49-86 (M07 beam is fire-only though 원소창 picks its element), SkillPresetExampleView.cs:62-98.\n15. Process: CLAUDE.md needs bilingual docs and en.txt keys; 92 icons need `.meta` guid checks; manifest/balance/wiki fingerprints (E).\n\nOpen questions (not decidable from code)\n1. Suspended runs, portals, `kitHero`, training records at migration: convert, refund, or keep the old engine?\n2. Flag scope: plan 14 keeps the release path unchanged until phase 7, yet phase 2 changes schema 22, cap 60, point=level. Which are gated; can a flag-off build read schema 22 (RC/GameStore.cs:62)?\n3. Old share codes and stored edict presets: reject, or remap and refund?\n4. HUD: modifier badge/name or description only? Modifier +1 from the quick popup during a run (D3 says invest only)?\n5. Result/telemetry credit for absorbed skills (W10->W09-1): base rows or modifier rows (`resultMetric`, `CombatTelemetry.Support`, RiftSkillShareView, Prototypes/RiftVictory)?\n6. Guide stage starts at hero level 1: where is Whirlwind taught after \"2 points\" (plan 15, branch codex/guide-tutorial-segment2)? Which first skill for ranger/mage (only the warrior has a stage)?\n7. Does the 18-slot layer keep M05 (index 16) and the four skill-reference options; may the 13 non-legacy actives be escape/defense skills?\n8. Non-owned training (`FullSkillTraining`, CombatSimulation.cs:14-15) at cap 60: which allocation?\n9. Legacy \"자동 행동 설계\"/\"성장과 스킬\" are inert for tree heroes (GameStore.BuildChanges.cs:26-32 re-projects `classSkills`): delete or leave?\n10. Retire Prototypes/SkillTree and its CI steps, or regenerate them?", "html": "<p>Prefixes (absolute): W=/Users/t8g-2410-pn-005/Documents/MyProject/HELLSCRIPT/wt-d4-skill-plan; RC=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Core; RP=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Runtime/Presentation; RR=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Resources; T=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Tests/Editor; E=W/Assets/HELLSCRIPT/Editor. Counts are my own greps unless marked (tool).<\/p><h2 id=\"0-reading-the-inventory\">0. Reading the inventory<\/h2><ul><li>Tool: 12,680 refs/475 files; groups 1-5 = 4,609 refs/133 files (<code>--check<\/code> exits 1). About 197 refs in 13 files are SVG path data (<code>M12 2 ...<\/code>, zero quoted ids): Prototypes RuneBoard html 148, Jeweler 12, RiftEntry/ui.js 5, AspectStone ui+svg 6, TrainingGround 8, Blacksmith 11, DailyQuests 3, tools/blacksmith/export-resources.cjs 4. Real prototype hits: SkillTree/<em>, HuntEdict/<\/em>, RiftVictory/{ui.js,build.cjs,source-manifest.json}, RiftEntry/engine.test.cjs, AspectStone/catalog.json.<\/li><li>It counts removed ids only. Blind spots, covered below: kept ids whose rules change (W01 becomes T2; A06/M07 change meaning), the version gate <code>ClassSkillTree.Uses<\/code> (55 sites/29 files), <code>ClassSkillTree.Unlocked<\/code> (17 non-smoke lines/11 files), level 30/40 literals, UI element names tutorials aim at.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"a-old-skill-windows\">A. Old skill window(s)<\/h2><p><strong>Builders.<\/strong> No standalone skill window exists; the tree is the &quot;skills&quot; tab of the unified edict window.<\/p><ul><li>RP/HuntEdictWindow.cs:40-51 <code>Open<\/code>: <code>Session.UseSkillTree(hero)<\/code> :48; <code>ContentWindowHost.Attach(view,view.HandleBack)<\/code> :49; <code>StoreViewBinding.Attach(view,store,view.Repaint,()=&gt;!HasDialog&amp;&amp;!HuntEdictOrderCard.Dragging,view.DisclosureDisplayKey)<\/code> :50 (key holds <code>StoreViewBinding.Key(hero.build.classSkills)<\/code>, HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:99-103). <code>DrawSkills()<\/code> :112; <code>HandleBack<\/code> :59-60; <code>SelectTab<\/code> :142; <code>SelectSkillPage<\/code> :152; draft model with Save/Revert footer :124-135, <code>Change<\/code> :173-179.<\/li><li>RP/HuntEdictWindow.Skills.cs (455 lines): <code>SelectSkill<\/code> :23; <code>DrawSkills<\/code> :35; <code>DrawTreePanel<\/code> :66 (list mode :71-76; tree mode :77-104 with Art/SkillTree/tree-backdrop + skill-point-gem); <code>DrawTreeCanvas<\/code> :106 and <code>DrawTreeNode<\/code> :208 (<code>SkillTreeLayout<\/code>, SkillTreeGraphic.cs:13-20); <code>ChangeRank/Equip/Unequip<\/code> :251-262; slot bubble :263-346; <code>OpenSkillPolicy<\/code> :348; <code>DrawSkillBar<\/code> :361 (4 actives + ultimate, <code>NodeFrame<\/code> :233-244); <code>DrawSkillDetails<\/code> :399 (inspector; buttons <code>edict-skill-rank-down|up|equip<\/code> :441-443; unlock rows :430-434).<\/li><li>Policy page HuntEdictWindow.SkillPresets.cs:54 (back button &quot;스킬 트리로&quot; :59; order :163-167; options :169-184); CombatPreview.cs (text &quot;레벨 40 · 스킬 1등급&quot; :90).<\/li><li><code>ShowLegacyEdictEditor<\/code> RP/GameUI.EdictEditor.cs:27: private <code>Base(&quot;edict&quot;)<\/code> page; <code>SkillName<\/code> = <code>game.catalog.skills.Single<\/code> :21 throws for ids outside the 18 legacy slots. Reached only from its own legacy share page (GameUI.EdictShare.cs:28) and 13 smokes: Runtime{Blizzard,Chain,Fireball,MageBasic,Nova,Ranger,Shield,Slam,Teleport,WarriorAttack,WarriorSupport}Smoke.cs:33, RuntimeTargetSmoke.cs:74, RuntimeLanguageSmoke.cs:183. Not tree UI; keep while those smokes live.<\/li><li>Other pickers: rift entry RP/RiftEntryWindow.cs:336-356 + Popups.cs:75-125 (learned candidates; <code>Store.ReplaceRiftSkill<\/code> RC/GameStore.RiftEntry.cs:39-51); training lobby TrainingGroundWindow.Skills.cs:12-62.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Entry points.<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Whole edict window: hub RP/GameUI.cs:242-244 and :446; dock GameUI.ContentDock.cs:31; observation menu GameUI.GlobalHud.cs:130; GameUI.{RiftVictory.cs:11, TrainingEquipment.cs:31, Comparison.cs:210-216 (loads a recorded loadout as draft), PuzzleHub.cs:41, Puzzle.cs:44, PuzzleOpening.cs:44, Tutorials.cs:105-110 (guides F06/H07/H08 target &quot;skills&quot;), FirstPlay.cs:19-23 (<code>SelectTab<\/code>+<code>SelectSkillPage(true)<\/code>+<code>SelectSkill(id)<\/code>), TrainingGround.cs:38-42 (<code>OpenSkillPolicy<\/code>)}.<\/li><li>Direct tree page (<code>ShowEdictSkillTree<\/code> GameUI.HuntEdict.cs:69): RiftEntryWindow.cs:355; SkillPresets.cs:59; HuntEdictWindow.cs:60. Not in plan 9.1: HuntEdictWindow.Presets.cs:96-99 (a stored preset whose allocation fails validation jumps to the skills tab). Recommended mode keeps the manage page editable (HuntEdictWindow.cs:85,147,176). No NPC/plaza route exists.<\/li><li>Smoke flags: one class gates eight (RP/RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:44: SkillTree, SkillReset, SkillMenu, SkillPreset, SkillCombatPreview, SkillIdentity, RegressionRepair, EdictSections); also <code>-hellscriptClassSkillSmoke<\/code> (RC/ClassSkillNativeSmoke.cs:38), BattleQuickEdit (RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke.cs:213), QuickPreset, GuideTutorial, Tutorial.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Reads/writes.<\/strong> Reads <code>store.Data<\/code>, <code>hero.build.classSkills<\/code>, rune levels <code>new HeroStats(hero,false,store.Data.runes).runeSkillLevels<\/code> (Skills.cs:19), <code>ClassSkillTree/ClassSkills/ClassSkillOptions<\/code>, <code>HuntEdictProgression<\/code>, <code>PuzzleTutorial<\/code>, <code>SkillProgressionInfo.Compare<\/code> (Skills.cs:436-438). Writes only via the commit lambda RP/GameUI.HuntEdict.cs:25-52 (4 contexts: comparison <code>ValidateB<\/code>+<code>ApplyHuntEdict<\/code>; training/puzzle <code>ApplyTrainingHuntEdict<\/code> or sandbox <code>game.PuzzleStore.CommitHuntEdict<\/code>; guide; normal/live <code>GameStore.CommitHuntEdict<\/code> RC/GameStore.HuntEdict.cs:9-62 with <code>PrepareHuntEdictChange<\/code>/<code>PrepareSuspendedHuntEdictChange<\/code>), plus <code>SetRecommendedEdict<\/code> (GameStore.Edict.cs:9) and immediate policy saves (<code>SaveSkillPolicy<\/code> RC/HuntEdictLoadout.cs:126-137). Every store edit API needs the selected hero (GameStore.HuntEdict.cs:13, GameStore.Edict.cs:13,30,61, GameStore.RiftEntry.cs:43): plan D2&#x27;s per-hero tabs need a new per-hero commit.<\/p><p><strong>Delete / keep / flag.<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Delete at phase 7: Skills.cs:66-104 tree branch and :106-230, <code>BandNames<\/code> :24, unlock rows :430-434, <code>SkillTreeLayout<\/code>, RR/Data/ClassSkillTree.json, Art/SkillTree/tree-backdrop + skill-point-gem (+E/ResourceTextureBudget.cs:33,76), en.txt:5286-5336, Prototypes/SkillTree, tools/build_skill_tree.cjs, RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke* (954 lines), SkillTreeIntegrationTests layout test (:207-214), caller-less <code>GameStore.CommitClassSkills<\/code> (RC/ClassSkillCodec.cs:69-81).<\/li><li>Keep: <code>SkillTreeGraphic<\/code> (glyphs HuntEdictWindow.Glyphs.cs:10, diagrams SkillPresetExampleView.cs:106), skill bar, slot bubble, policy page, order editor, Art/SkillTree/node-frame-*.<\/li><li>Keep or port: the tutorial list-mode UI (<code>DrawAvailableSkills<\/code> HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:35-45; inspector +/equip; guards Skills.cs:23,251-252). Plan 12 says only &quot;tree and inspector&quot;; four tutorial files aim at these names (C).<\/li><li>Flag at: <code>ShowEdictSkillTree<\/code>, <code>DrawSkills<\/code>, RiftEntryWindow.cs:355, FirstPlay.cs:22, SkillPresets.cs:59 (label must stop saying &quot;skill tree&quot;), Presets.cs:99, Tutorials.cs:110, TrainingGround.cs:41.<\/li><li>Hazard, not in plan: the edict window&#x27;s <code>HuntEdictEditSession<\/code> is built once (HuntEdictWindow.cs:48) and refreshed only by its own commit (GameStore.HuntEdict.cs:59); <code>StoreViewBinding<\/code> just calls <code>Repaint<\/code> (:50,138-141), which redraws the stale draft. A D4 window above it that commits would be reverted by the parent&#x27;s next Save, and the parent&#x27;s equip bar shows old ranks. The parent must <code>AcceptSaved<\/code>/rebuild after each child commit.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"b-battle-quick-edit-hud-recommended-skills-pr-83-huntedictquickmenu-gameuiedictquickskillquick-globalhudview-holdpress-runtimebattlequickeditsmoke-the-potion-quick-files-hold-no-skill-logic\">B. Battle quick edit, HUD, recommended skills (PR #83: HuntEdictQuickMenu, GameUI.{EdictQuick,SkillQuick}, GlobalHudView, HoldPress, RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke; the potion quick files hold no skill logic)<\/h2><p><strong>Today.<\/strong> HUD slots: 3 potions, 4 actives, 1 ultimate (RP/GlobalHudView.cs:58-60,128-131). Tap -&gt; <code>SkillSlotTapped<\/code> (RP/GameUI.SkillQuick.cs:21-39): candidates = learned, unequipped skills of the slot kind (<code>HuntEdictQuickMenu.SkillCandidates<\/code> RC/HuntEdictQuickMenu.cs:57-58; slot 4 = ultimates), then, while a point is free, level/lineage-unlocked rank-0 skills (<code>LearnableSkills<\/code> :60-61, drawn dim, SkillQuick.cs:36). Tap a candidate -&gt; <code>EquipQuickSkill<\/code> :84-96 (<code>ClassSkillTree.Equip<\/code> + <code>CommitHuntEdict(session,catalog,game.Combat,true)<\/code>). Hold (0.3 s + 0.7 s gauge) -&gt; <code>ShowSkillPopup<\/code> :97-126 (<code>ClassSkillDisplay.Description<\/code>; &quot;레벨 올리기&quot; = <code>RankQuickSkill<\/code> :127-137, base +1 only; &quot;장착&quot;; use presets). Only in ordinary rift fights (<code>QuickBattleEditable<\/code>, GameUI.EdictQuick.cs:24-32) or the guide stage; <code>SkillQuickAvailable<\/code> (SkillQuick.cs:19) uses <code>ClassSkillTree.Uses<\/code> (= v3/v4), so a v5 loadout silently disables it. Display: <code>GlobalHudSnapshot.Read<\/code> fills skills only for v3/v4 (RP/GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:86-103); <code>HudSlotState<\/code> (:9-14) has no rank/modifier; icon <code>SkillIconAssets.TryResolve<\/code> (GlobalHudView.cs:140, SkillIconView.cs:57-71); cooldown = radial <code>Cover<\/code> + <code>TimeLabel<\/code> (GlobalHudView.cs:143-146). The HUD does not choose &quot;recommended skills&quot;. The recommended things are: <code>useRecommendedEdict<\/code> (RC/HuntEdictDefaults.cs:11-34: keeps allocation/slots, clears <code>options<\/code>/<code>presetSelections<\/code>, automatic = all); <code>FirstPlayRecommendation<\/code> skill steps (RC/FirstPlayRecommendation.cs:28-40); legacy &quot;현재 레벨 추천&quot; <code>BehaviorPresets.ForLevel<\/code> (GameUI.Growth.cs:49-72; level clamp 1-30, BehaviorPresets.cs:13; not tree-aware); 122 use presets (RR/HuntEdictQuickPresets.json) and the &quot;identity&quot; order (RC/HuntEdictQuickPresets.cs:112). <strong>Changes.<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Modifier chosen: add <code>rank/modifier/modifierRank<\/code> to <code>ClassSkillStatus<\/code> (RC/ClassSkillReadModel.cs:7-14) and <code>HudSlotState<\/code>. <code>TryResolve<\/code> returns false for <code>W01-3<\/code> (no <code>ClassSkills.Find<\/code>; a 5-char id misses the legacy branches :63-70): add a <code>&lt;base&gt;-&lt;n&gt;<\/code> branch (art <code>Art/ClassSkillIcons/&lt;Class&gt;/&lt;id&gt;<\/code>) if a badge is wanted. Put modifier name + shape sentence + n/5 into <code>ClassSkillDisplay.Description/Activation<\/code> (RC/ClassSkillDisplay.cs:9-31), used by the HUD (GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:94,99), popup (SkillQuick.cs:102), rift-entry popup (RiftEntryWindow.Popups.cs:105-107). Popup: &quot;+1 on the chosen modifier / pick one&quot; and the plan&#x27;s blocked reasons; swap/refund only in town (D3). First fix <code>ClassSkillTree.Display<\/code>: its regex matches <code>A06<\/code> inside <code>A06-2<\/code> (ClassSkillTree.cs:119-120). Other icon/name sites: TrainingGroundWindow.Skills.cs:53-58, RiftSkillShareView.cs:35, TrainingChartView.cs:62,113-114, StatusStripView.cs:109, GameUI.GlobalHud.cs:51-55, toast SkillQuick.cs:94; <code>TrainingGround.DescribeChanges<\/code> (RC/TrainingGround.cs:214-229) should diff modifier/rank. HUD badge vs name is undecided in the plan.<\/li><li>Unlearned: restate the v4 rule &quot;unlearned cannot be equipped&quot; (RC/ClassSkills.cs:123) for v5; rank 0 clears the slot (ClassSkillTree.cs:114-115) and must be refused while the modifier holds rank; candidates already skip rank 0 (HuntEdictQuickMenu.cs:58). <code>Unlocked(load,level,id)<\/code> is level+lineage; the (hero,level,id) overload (ClassSkillTree.cs:60; Tutorials.Progress.cs:17) cannot express tier gates. HUD <code>locked<\/code> (GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:94) loses meaning.<\/li><li>Ultimate rank 3: <code>RankScale<\/code> is 1 for ultimates (RC/ClassSkills.cs:65; used ClassSkillDisplay.cs:19, ClassSkillReadModel.cs:22,26). Cooldown 60/55/50 reaches the HUD via <code>CS.ultimateTotal<\/code> (ClassSkillReadModel.cs:25; <code>Max(45,cd)<\/code> at CombatSimulation.ClassSkills.cs:163); persistence accepts totals 45-60 (ClassSkillPersistence.cs:26) and rankScale 1..1.401 (:37), so +20%/rank (1.4 at rank 3) fits by 0.001. Replace &quot;Lv.40&quot; gates by &quot;T5 open or learned&quot;: GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:99, HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:33, RiftEntryWindow.cs:338,345,349,356, TrainingGroundWindow.Skills.cs:42, Tutorials.cs:56,214, en.txt:5758,5837.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"c-tutorials-and-guide\">C. Tutorials and guide<\/h2><p>Live flows: guide stage (flow 6; new accounts, warrior only: RC/GameStore.Guide.cs:11, RP/GameController.Tutorials.cs:16); puzzle (flow 5; accounts mid-puzzle plus every replay/hub: GameController.Tutorials.cs:17-20,50); pit/starter (old checkpoints only, RC/Tutorials.cs:153-169).<\/p><ul><li>Guide stage: <code>GuideTutorial.Skill=&quot;W01&quot;<\/code> (RC/GuideTutorial.cs:13), <code>BarePowers<\/code>=<code>ResetAllocation<\/code> (:52-57), <code>LessonDone<\/code> :77, <code>StartGuideTutorial<\/code> GameStore.Guide.cs:18, copy/anchors &quot;회오리&quot;, &quot;스킬 포인트가 1점&quot; (RP/GameUI.GuideTutorial.cs:36,70,94-102; <code>edict-quick-skill-*<\/code> names), fingerprint &quot;tutorial-v6&quot; (GuideTutorial.cs:12-13; mismatching checkpoints are dropped, Tutorials.cs:163). W01 is T2 (gate 2; skill_tree_d4.json rules.tierGates [0,2,6,11,40]), so the level-1 point cannot buy it. Rebase on W09 (plan D7): change <code>Skill<\/code>, copy, Version/Fingerprint; teach W01 only at 2+1 points (hero level 3); update RuntimeGuideTutorialSmoke, GuideTutorialTests (3).<\/li><li>Prologue/starter/pit: <code>PrologueSkill/StarterComparison<\/code> hard-code W01/A01/M01 + presets stand/edge, elite/steady, steady/pack (RC/Tutorials.cs:98-101). Consumers: <code>ProloguePowers<\/code> (GameStore.Tutorials.cs:33-48: <code>ChangeRank<\/code> on a T2 skill at level 1 throws), <code>CanAdvancePrologueLesson<\/code> :93-100, CombatPreviewSession.cs:41-49, CombatSimulation.SkillPreview.cs:16-26, HuntEdictProgression.cs:101-102,165-168 (level-1 &quot;first skill only&quot;, <code>owner.level&gt;=2<\/code>), HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:37-38,90-98. Needs a T1 starter per class: W09/W08, A07/A14, M07 (mage has one T1 active).<\/li><li>Overlays aim at old-window element names: RP/GameUI.TutorialStaging.cs:259-323, PuzzleOpening.cs:50-61, TutorialPit.cs:113-122, TutorialComparison.cs:10-29 (<code>edict-skill-&lt;id&gt;<\/code>, <code>edict-skill-rank-up|equip<\/code>, <code>edict-active-slot-0<\/code>, <code>edict-slot-policy<\/code>, <code>edict-policy-back<\/code>, <code>edict-preset-tab-*<\/code>, <code>edict-preset-activate<\/code>). Keep the lesson-mode UI or retarget four files.<\/li><li>Puzzle (16 levels): RR/PuzzleTutorial.json kits, e.g. level 7: W01 W02 WP01 W03 / A01 A02 AP01 A03 A04 / M01 M02 MP01 M03 M04 at hero level &lt;=7. W02 is T4, A03/A04/M04 T3, WP01 unlocks Lv4 (hero is 3 at puzzle 4), MP01 is removed (13 refs). Granted by <code>ClassSkillTree.ChangeRank<\/code> (RC/PuzzleTutorial.cs:100 <code>Instructor<\/code>, :150-163 <code>StartPowers<\/code>), validated :208-211 (<code>rank&gt;1<\/code> forbidden): needs a kit/exempt API. Also GameUI.Puzzle.cs:18-30,57,72-76, CombatSimulation.Tutorial.cs:133,148,170. Saved loadouts: <code>puzzle.levels[].kitHero<\/code> (replay source PuzzleTutorial.cs:225-228), T/Fixtures/PuzzleAfterL8-{Mage,Ranger,Warrior}.json (553 refs; PuzzleContentTests.cs:94, PuzzleTutorialCoreTests.cs:26).<\/li><li>F06/H07/H08/H17: RC/Tutorials.cs:33 (F06 copy &quot;2레벨부터 받는 스킬 포인트&quot;), :55-56 (H08 &quot;레벨 40&quot;), :214-217; Tutorials.Progress.cs:10-18 (F06 = open active never slotted, level&gt;=2), :51-59 (H07 on <code>Spent<\/code> growth, H08 on ultimate); TutorialChapters.cs C05 {F06,H07}; FirstPlayRecommendation.cs:28-40; docs Tutorial_Progression.md:15,67-80. New rule: the first T2 skill needs 2 points in T1/passives = hero level 3 for every class, so the &quot;level-2 point&quot; premise (Tutorials.Progress.cs:10-12) is false and <code>NewSkills<\/code> needs the allocation, not level. <code>ClassPracticeLesson.cs:9,28<\/code> (A02/M02, both T2) must test &quot;learned&quot;.<\/li><li>New-player start: <code>StartNewHeroesWithoutSkills<\/code>+<code>ActivateSkillTrees<\/code> (RC/GameStore.SkillTree.cs:13-47; callers GameController.cs:65,238, GameController.Accounts.cs:23, GameUI.RiftKeeper.cs:15; skips heroes with a suspended run :30,34) emit v3/v4.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"d-auto-battle--hunt-edict\">D. Auto-battle / Hunt Edict<\/h2><ul><li>Two layers. Legacy V2 document: 4 slots, <code>skillOrder<\/code>, option sets for 01-06 only (<code>HuntEdict.SkillIds<\/code> RC/HuntEdict.cs:56; HuntEdictV2.Options.cs:40-129; rule conditions, EdictValidation.cs:53); tree loadouts project into it only for <code>LegacyIndex&gt;=0<\/code> ids (RC/ClassSkills.cs:150-161). Of 30 retained actives 17 are legacy-index; 13 are not (W08 W09 W17 W18 A07 A14 A17 A18 M07 M08 M11 M17 M18): they use <code>ClassSkillOptions<\/code> (55 groups/166 choices; 25/74 sit on removed actives) and cannot be picked by <code>survival.defenseSkill|escapeSkill|fallbackSkill<\/code>, <code>explore.cursedDefense<\/code> (EdictOptions.cs:63,70; HUD choices from <code>edict.slots<\/code>, HuntEdictHudRows.cs:23), which still list M05.<\/li><li>Removed-id hits: HuntEdictV2.Options.cs:117-120 (M05), HuntEdictV2.Order.cs:49 (<code>BuffSkill<\/code>), :51,63,89 (compiled <code>edict:M05<\/code>, slot 16), HuntEdictV2.Availability.cs:50 (needs WP03), :73, :75; <code>UnlockLevel<\/code> use :27,35; HuntEdictV2.cs:91,94.<\/li><li>Presets/scenarios change atomically: RR/HuntEdictQuickPresets.json 211 presets (122 skill, 50 on removed ids; 76 global; 9 basic; 4 order); RR/SkillPresetScenarios.json 122 scenarios (50 removed); <code>SkillPresetScenario.All<\/code> throws unless every non-passive catalog skill has exactly one scenario per preset (RC/SkillPresetScenario.cs:52-53). SkillPresetExampleView.cs:62-98 has M05/M13 scenes.<\/li><li>Saved policy ids: <code>presetSelections<\/code> for <code>skill/&lt;removed&gt;<\/code> make <code>ClassSkillLoadout.Canonical<\/code> throw (RC/HuntEdictSkillPresets.cs:19,22-35), unknown <code>options<\/code> throw (ClassSkillOptions.cs:46-52). Plan 7 filters <code>order/automatic/options<\/code> only; also filter <code>presetSelections<\/code>, <code>legacyEdict<\/code> (slots, skillOrder, survival refs), <code>actives<\/code>, <code>ultimate<\/code>, <code>ranks<\/code>.<\/li><li><code>ClassSkillValidationBuild<\/code>: 30 builds in ClassSkills.json (29 touch removed ids); <code>CreateClassSkillValidation<\/code> (RC/CombatSimulation.ClassSkillValidation.cs:29-58) writes level 40 + free-form actives/passives/ultimate under <code>classSkillValidation<\/code>; <code>CreateSkillPreview<\/code> does likewise (CombatSimulation.SkillPreview.cs:31-38). Tier/point rules need an explicit fixture bypass. Users: T/ClassSkillCompatibilityTests.cs:18-26, ClassSkillPassiveMeasurement.cs:188.<\/li><li>Recommended-edict defaults: <code>HuntEdictDefaults.Skills<\/code> keeps allocation (a modifier rides along); <code>SetRecommendedEdict<\/code> is selected-hero only (GameStore.Edict.cs:9-22).<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"e-tooling-docs-localization-art\">E. Tooling, docs, localization, art<\/h2><ul><li>CI .github/workflows/class-skills.yml:22-29: <code>class_skill_runtime.py check<\/code> (111/123/60/55, :24-25,42); <code>class_skills.py check<\/code> (16/19/2 per class :42; 111/141 :38; ultimate unlock 40 rank 1 :48; 30 builds :69; sha256 of GameCatalog.cs, SkillEffects.cs, SkillProgression.cs, Itemization.cs, LegendaryPowers.json, ClassSetReference/catalog.json :97-113); <code>class_skill_options.py check<\/code> (55/166 :10,49); <code>class_skill_reports.py check<\/code> (90 builds + 18 <code>M13=<\/code>/<code>W02=<\/code> runs :25-34); <code>node Prototypes/SkillTree/build.cjs<\/code> + <code>git diff --exit-code<\/code> (embeds sha256 of ClassSkills.json and Docs/Design/ClassSkills/catalog.json, build.cjs:5-13); <code>node tools/build_skill_tree.cjs --check<\/code>; <code>node Prototypes/SkillTree/engine.test.cjs<\/code>. All fail on the first data edit. shared-ui.yml:19 runs <code>check_ui_contract.py --verify<\/code> (ADAPTERS :16-23; rules :63-77: unregistered <code>*Window<\/code>, Canvas owners, hex literals).<\/li><li>Pipeline: Docs/Design/ClassSkills/{catalog,runtime_parameters,use_options}.json -&gt; RR/Data/ClassSkills.json; Prototypes/SkillTree -&gt; RR/Data/ClassSkillTree.json. Generated docs: Docs/Design/HELLSCRIPT_{Warrior,Ranger,Mage}_Skills(.en).md, HELLSCRIPT_Skill_Equipment(.en).md, Class_Skill_Use_Policies(.en).md. Inventory group 6: 342 files/8,071 refs.<\/li><li>balance_1000.py:222-231 (sha256 of ClassSkills.cs, GameStore.SkillTree.cs, ClassSkillTree.cs, GameStore.cs, Economy.cs, HeroStats.Blacksmith.cs, ClassSkills.json, ClassSkillTree.json); Balance1000/production_skill_tree_audit.json (<code>skillTreeVersion:3, levelCap:40<\/code>) read by test_balance_1000.py:19-25. wiki.py:143-163, :302 (<code>skills:18,passives:18<\/code>), :690-714 (<code>tree_levels[id]<\/code> KeyError; titles &quot;108/164/55&quot; :712-714,796-799); test_wiki.py:37-46,134-135 (:84&#x27;s 108 = legendaries, unaffected). generate_sfx.py:83-86 + T/SoundBankTests.cs:150 + ClassSkillRuntimeTests.Audio.cs:12 (a <code>skill.&lt;id&gt;<\/code> sound per non-passive skill); audit_equipment_art.py:51; class_set_reference.py:38,55 and legendary_catalog.py:30 (ids limited to 01-06).<\/li><li>Localization: en.txt:5286-5336 (old tree), 20 lines naming removed skills (503-505, 1218-1220, 1679-1680, 1802-1803, 2126, 2133, 6460; :124 WP03), level-40 lines 5758, 5837, 6356. Names/descriptions live in ClassSkills.json (name/nameEn), GameCatalog.cs:466-484 and <code>GameCatalog.Passives<\/code> via <code>Loc.T<\/code> (GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:72), not in en.txt.<\/li><li>Art: 37 icons per class in RR/Art/ClassSkillIcons (A06/M07 are overwritten: check <code>.meta<\/code> guid); fallbacks RR/Art/GlobalHUD/passive-* and Art/SkillAtlas.png (SkillIconView.cs:63-70; T/HuntEdictFoundationTests.cs:215-231 loops the 12 legacy ids per class); Docs/Art/ClassSkillIcons/manifest.json (111; assemble_manifest.py:15 <code>pass==111<\/code>); E/ResourceTextureBudget.cs:24 already covers <code>Art/ClassSkillIcons/<\/code>; BuildResourceTests.cs:11, RuntimeBuildResourceSmoke.cs:21.<\/li><li>asmdef: one runtime asmdef (Core+Presentation+Runes) and Hellscript.Tests.asmdef absorb new files; only <code>.meta<\/code> files are needed.<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"f-smokes-and-editmode-tests\">F. Smokes and EditMode tests<\/h2><p>Smokes: 158 files (157 RP/Runtime<em>Smoke<\/em>.cs + RC/ClassSkillNativeSmoke.cs): 30 touch the old window API, 7 only removed ids, 8 only tree API, 113 untouched.<\/p><ul><li>Replace: RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke{,.CombatPreview,.Identity,.Presets,.Sections}.cs (954 lines, 8 flags) -&gt; <code>-hellscriptSkillTreeD4Smoke<\/code>. First move <code>ExistingTrees<\/code>/<code>OpenEdict<\/code> (RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:23-37; builds <code>version=3<\/code> loadouts) to a shared fixture: 8 call sites in 7 files (RuntimeRiftEntrySmoke .cs/.Portal/.Pickers/.Preparation/.Repeat, EdictQuickPresetSmoke:105, TrainingGroundSmoke:121).<\/li><li>Port: EdictQuickPreset (18 hits), Tutorial{,.Puzzle,.Pit}, GuideTutorial, RecommendedEquipment.Controls, RiftEntry*, BattleQuickEdit{,.Order} (setup learns every &quot;unlocked&quot; skill, :227-234), EdictContract, Edict, Language, UiStyle, TrainingGround{,.SafeDodge}, TrainingEquipment, Target; id-bound: ClassSkillNativeSmoke (25 refs), Shield (M05/MP04), Ranger, WarriorAttack, ArtGallery, RiftVictory{,.Actions}, Effect, Passive, Charge (text).<\/li><li>Stay while <code>ShowLegacyEdictEditor<\/code> stays: Blizzard, Chain, Fireball, MageBasic, Nova, Slam, Teleport, WarriorSupport.<\/li><\/ul><p>EditMode: 249 files, 4,518 cases (~2,731 methods); 29 files/462 refs name removed ids (101 methods in 27 files); ~64 files/~248 methods use tree/tutorial/preset APIs.<\/p><ul><li>Delete or rewrite (pin old rules): SkillTreeIntegrationTests (17 methods/42 cases; layout :207-214, counts :59,68), ClassSkillRuntimeTests.cs:56-59 (37/16/19), ClassSkillBoundaryTests.cs:48,69 (37 ranks, cap 30), ClassSkillPassiveTests.cs:124, ClassSkillPolicyTests.cs:58 (55 options), HuntEdictFoundationTests.cs:198-231.<\/li><li>Port (methods): GuideTutorial 3, TutorialProgression 18, FirstPlaySkill 6, FirstPlayExperience 7, TutorialChapter 6, TutorialHeroSlots 9, Puzzle{Content 5, Opening 9, TutorialCore 10, Graduation 15, Level 1}, HuntEdict{Progression 20, QuickMenu 9, QuickPreset 5, SkillPreset 9, Overview 10, SuspendedSave 6, Defaults 5}, SkillPresetCombatPreview 10, TrainingGround 20, TrainingGroundUi 12, RecommendedEquipment (codec :210,239-242), ClassSkillCompatibility 7.<\/li><li>Engine-bound, id-bound (out of scope): ClassSkillPolicy 12 methods, ClassSkillRuntimeTests.Identity 12, .Contributions 9, EdictShield 9, Effect 8, EdictResponse 7, others 1-4 each.<\/li><li>Stay: the rest (~2,480 methods), incl. <code>ContentTestAccounts<\/code> (62 files; legacy 18-slot path).<\/li><\/ul><h2 id=\"g-fifteen-places-most-likely-to-be-forgotten-risk-order\">G. Fifteen places most likely to be forgotten (risk order)<\/h2><ol><li>CI class-skills.yml (7 steps, E) goes red on the first catalog edit; Prototypes/SkillTree/build.cjs hashes ClassSkills.json.<\/li><li>Save read throws for any v3/v4 loadout invalid in the new catalog: RC/GameStore.cs:159-163 (<code>hero.build<\/code>), :166 and :413-414 (suspended run), :170-187 (<code>presets[]<\/code>). Migrate before <code>Normalize<\/code> and cover every holder: <code>edictPresets[].loadout<\/code>, <code>edictLegacyBuild<\/code>, <code>trainingGround.records[].{previous,best}.loadout<\/code> (RC/TrainingGround.cs:33), <code>trainingComparison.baselineHeroJson<\/code>, <code>puzzle.levels[].kitHero<\/code>, <code>tutorialRun/tutorialSlots<\/code>; filter presetSelections/options/legacyEdict too (D). Plan 7 names <code>hero<\/code> and <code>order/automatic/options<\/code> only.<\/li><li>Suspended run/portal: <code>ActivateSkillTrees<\/code> skips such heroes (GameStore.SkillTree.cs:30,34) while <code>ClassSkillPersistence.ValidateRun<\/code> throws on cooldown/cast/effect ids of removed skills (:33,37,42,48: W15 loan, M13 channel, W02/M13 intent): the portal run becomes unreadable.<\/li><li><code>ClassSkillTree.Uses<\/code> (v3|v4, ClassSkillTree.cs:25) gates 55 sites: HUD (GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:86), quick edit (SkillQuick.cs:19), <code>UsesTree<\/code>, HeroStats (Economy.cs:129), TrainingGround.cs:37,214, ClassSkills.cs:60: all go silent for v5.<\/li><li>Two writers of <code>classSkills<\/code> (stale parent session, A hazard) and no per-hero commit (A); the commit lambda has 4 contexts (GameUI.HuntEdict.cs:25-52).<\/li><li>Tutorial overlays bound to old element names + the lesson-mode UI (C).<\/li><li>Hand-built fixtures assume free-form loadouts: RuntimeSkillTreeSmoke.cs:29-37, CombatSimulation.SkillPreview.cs:31-38, ClassSkillValidation.cs:33-39, PuzzleTutorial.cs:95-108,147-176, GuideTutorial.cs:52-57, GameStore.Tutorials.cs:33-48, PuzzleAfterL8 fixtures: give the v5 validator one explicit kit/fixture path.<\/li><li>Share codes: <code>ClassSkillCodec.Decode<\/code> demands byte-exact canonical JSON (RC/ClassSkillCodec.cs:19-52; wrapped by HuntEdictPresetCodec.cs:29-36,53-54), so new <code>modifier<\/code> fields break every existing HED4/HED5 code unless an old-wire branch exists (tests ClassSkillBoundaryTests.cs:46-49, RecommendedEquipmentTests.cs:210,239-242, ClassSkillPassiveTests.cs:124-132).<\/li><li>Pinned counts: ClassSkills.cs:52-56 (111/123/60, unlock&lt;=40), SkillPresetScenario.cs:52-53, ClassSkillOptions.cs:46 (&lt;=55), plus E/F. Old and new catalogs cannot coexist behind the flag until versioned (6 key passives already push 111 up).<\/li><li>30/40 literals missing from plan 4: ClassSkills.cs:137,147; GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:99; HuntEdictWindow.Progression.cs:33; RiftEntryWindow.cs:345,349,356; GameUI.Growth.cs:20,36 (cap 30); BehaviorPresets.cs:13; CombatSimulation.SkillPreview.cs:31, ClassSkillValidation.cs:33; HuntEdictWindow.CombatPreview.cs:90; ClassSkillTree.cs:42 (cache key <code>class*41+level<\/code>); CombatSimulation.cs:14-15 + Economy.cs:128 (non-owned training uses LevelCap as hero level); Tutorials.cs:56,214.<\/li><li><code>ClassSkillTree.UnlockLevel<\/code> (:30) feeds engine LEVEL_LOCK (CombatSimulation.ClassSkills.cs:24) and HuntEdictV2Availability (:27); tiers have no unlock level.<\/li><li>ID plumbing: <code>SkillIconAssets.TryResolve<\/code>, <code>ClassSkillTree.Display<\/code> regex, <code>ClassSkills.Find<\/code> null for <code>W01-3<\/code>; <code>ClassSkills.Find(skill).legacy<\/code> NREs for scopes naming removed ids (HuntEdictQuickPresets.cs:122,185, HuntEdictSkillPresets.cs:75).<\/li><li>Legacy screens under-report because <code>build.activeSkills<\/code> holds only legacy ids: GameUI.SettingsInformation.cs:31-34, Presets.cs:88, Growth.cs:19-49, History.cs:16-17; legendary &quot;requiredSkill Lv.N&quot; text (InventoryLayout.cs:188-193); RuneMasteryCatalog.cs:59-61 and <code>runeSkillLevels[18]<\/code> (gear/rune +rank reaches only the 17 retained legacy-index actives; plan D5).<\/li><li>Presentation keyed by old ids: GlobalHudSnapshot.cs:135-147, GameAudio.Combat.cs:21-27 + RR/Audio/Sfx/bank.json (30 refs), WorldView.SkillFx.cs:49-86 (M07 beam is fire-only though 원소창 picks its element), SkillPresetExampleView.cs:62-98.<\/li><li>Process: CLAUDE.md needs bilingual docs and en.txt keys; 92 icons need <code>.meta<\/code> guid checks; manifest/balance/wiki fingerprints (E).<\/li><\/ol><p>Open questions (not decidable from code)<\/p><ol><li>Suspended runs, portals, <code>kitHero<\/code>, training records at migration: convert, refund, or keep the old engine?<\/li><li>Flag scope: plan 14 keeps the release path unchanged until phase 7, yet phase 2 changes schema 22, cap 60, point=level. Which are gated; can a flag-off build read schema 22 (RC/GameStore.cs:62)?<\/li><li>Old share codes and stored edict presets: reject, or remap and refund?<\/li><li>HUD: modifier badge/name or description only? Modifier +1 from the quick popup during a run (D3 says invest only)?<\/li><li>Result/telemetry credit for absorbed skills (W10-&gt;W09-1): base rows or modifier rows (<code>resultMetric<\/code>, <code>CombatTelemetry.Support<\/code>, RiftSkillShareView, Prototypes/RiftVictory)?<\/li><li>Guide stage starts at hero level 1: where is Whirlwind taught after &quot;2 points&quot; (plan 15, branch codex/guide-tutorial-segment2)? Which first skill for ranger/mage (only the warrior has a stage)?<\/li><li>Does the 18-slot layer keep M05 (index 16) and the four skill-reference options; may the 13 non-legacy actives be escape/defense skills?<\/li><li>Non-owned training (<code>FullSkillTraining<\/code>, CombatSimulation.cs:14-15) at cap 60: which allocation?<\/li><li>Legacy &quot;자동 행동 설계&quot;/&quot;성장과 스킬&quot; are inert for tree heroes (GameStore.BuildChanges.cs:26-32 re-projects <code>classSkills<\/code>): delete or leave?<\/li><li>Retire Prototypes/SkillTree and its CI steps, or regenerate them?<\/li><\/ol>", "headings": [{"id": "0-reading-the-inventory", "title": "0. Reading the inventory"}, {"id": "a-old-skill-windows", "title": "A. Old skill window(s)"}, {"id": "b-battle-quick-edit-hud-recommended-skills-pr-83-huntedictquickmenu-gameuiedictquickskillquick-globalhudview-holdpress-runtimebattlequickeditsmoke-the-potion-quick-files-hold-no-skill-logic", "title": "B. Battle quick edit, HUD, recommended skills (PR #83: HuntEdictQuickMenu, GameUI.{EdictQuick,SkillQuick}, GlobalHudView, HoldPress, RuntimeBattleQuickEditSmoke; the potion quick files hold no skill logic)"}, {"id": "c-tutorials-and-guide", "title": "C. Tutorials and guide"}, {"id": "d-auto-battle--hunt-edict", "title": "D. Auto-battle / Hunt Edict"}, {"id": "e-tooling-docs-localization-art", "title": "E. Tooling, docs, localization, art"}, {"id": "f-smokes-and-editmode-tests", "title": "F. Smokes and EditMode tests"}, {"id": "g-fifteen-places-most-likely-to-be-forgotten-risk-order", "title": "G. Fifteen places most likely to be forgotten (risk order)"}]}];
